From: RenoDX AMD bridge experiment
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dlss: route Streamline DLSS input to FidelityFX on AMD

Target baseline: clshortfuse/renodx@8d360960a8bdeccada1a1babf7f02215c15c82e8
Reviewed against current streamline_v2.hpp layout as of 2026-08-31.

This patch is intentionally fail-open. NVIDIA systems keep the existing RenoDX
Streamline path. The alternate backend only reports DLSS support after the AMD
DX12 device and a FidelityFX upscaler provider have both been validated.

New files to copy into src/utils/dlss/:
- amd_bridge.hpp
- ffx_runtime_loader.hpp
- ffx_upscale_backend_dx12.hpp

The Streamline integration changes below:
- initialize FidelityFX from a queried native D3D12 device after slSetD3DDevice
- keep AMD state scoped by frame token + viewport
- capture tags after RenoDX clone redirection
- capture common constants and DLSS options
- virtualize the three DLSS feature functions needed by typical integrations
- offer DLSS evaluation to FidelityFX before NVIDIA Streamline
- only fall through before AMD GPU work has started
- shut the AMD backend down before Streamline shutdown

