Known PoC limitations intentionally NOT hidden by this patch:
- slIsFeatureSupported called before slSetD3DDevice cannot yet validate the AMD
  provider and therefore still falls through to Streamline.
- slGetFeatureRequirements/version virtualization is not implemented yet.
- slInit feature filtering is not implemented; some titles may reject AMD before
  the device hook if they require the NVIDIA DLSS plugin during initialization.
- frame-time delta is currently a backend configuration default until RenoDX
  supplies measured per-frame timing.
- non-zero Streamline resource-subrect offsets fail preflight rather than dispatch
  against the wrong pixels.
- the source files require the official FidelityFX SDK headers and runtime DLLs;
  see BUILD_INTEGRATION.md.

